// PURPOSE: Turn the saved transformation queries into automatic processing.
//
// An update policy runs when new rows arrive in RawTelemetry. Each policy calls
// one function and writes its result to the table named above the policy.
// Several policies can react to the same incoming message, so the main message,
// its zones, and drift observations can be produced independently.
//
// IsTransactional:false is a deliberate availability choice. If a conversion
// fails, the original message still reaches RawTelemetry and can be replayed,
// but the affected clean table may temporarily miss that row. Production use
// therefore requires the failure monitoring shown in 09-monitoring.kql.

// Automatically populate ControllerTelemetry from matching raw messages.
.alter table ControllerTelemetry policy update
```
[{"IsEnabled":true,"Source":"RawTelemetry","Query":"TransformControllerTelemetry()","IsTransactional":false,"PropagateIngestionProperties":true}]
```

// Automatically populate GatewayTelemetry from matching raw messages.
.alter table GatewayTelemetry policy update
```
[{"IsEnabled":true,"Source":"RawTelemetry","Query":"TransformGatewayTelemetry()","IsTransactional":false,"PropagateIngestionProperties":true}]
```

// Automatically populate the main cooling-unit table.
.alter table CoolingUnitTelemetry policy update
```
[{"IsEnabled":true,"Source":"RawTelemetry","Query":"TransformCoolingUnitTelemetry()","IsTransactional":false,"PropagateIngestionProperties":true}]
```

// Independently create one child row for every cooling-unit zone.
.alter table CoolingUnitZones policy update
```
[{"IsEnabled":true,"Source":"RawTelemetry","Query":"TransformCoolingUnitZones()","IsTransactional":false,"PropagateIngestionProperties":true}]
```
